# A copy proposal's occurrence is trusted by how far it agrees with the context back past the matched suffix: with
# L=1 (default) the occurrence proposed is the one of the latest 64 (with enough tokens after them) whose agreement
# runs furthest back, ties the latest; a proposal agreeing for fewer than LO tokens proposes at most K drafts.
# Only proposals change: a round keeps the drafts that equal the serial sample (multi._round's keep loop), so replies
# are the same bits under any proposal (as F44's policy sweep showed for depth policies). Policy class, not numerics.
# Measured offline (copysim.py, the engine's own copy_drafts.CopyDrafts replayed round by round over real
# GLM-5.3-Flash agent replies from the owner's omp sessions, prompts capped at 600k tokens): production's copy rounds
# keep 8.5 tokens in 16-row windows (49.9% of drafts), 15% keep only the sampled token; proposals agreeing for under
# 8 tokens (56%) keep 6.6 on average, 128+ keep 14.5. With 16:7, on three disjoint samples (1,556 / 1,556 / 1,883
# replies, 327-417k tokens), decode time against production: one stream (concave batched window table) +1.0..+1.3%,
# a stream's share of a 4-stream round (29 ms + 1.95 a row) +4.8..+6.2%, under every DFlash2 tokens-a-round
# assumption for the uncopied positions (realdec code 3.63, prose 2.78, a full block 8); with TF_GLM_COPY_MISS_MAX=7
# beside it +1.1..+1.3% / +5.5..+6.9%. Host cost: +0..+12 us a proposal at 600k contexts (paired, bench_copy_agree.py).
# The startup comparison carries the setting (CopySettings.code() 7 ints; engine's off-case padded to match).
# Test: test_copy_agree.py (CPU): off = the synced tree's proposals over 460 real + synthetic streams; on = an
# independent implementation (copysim.Tiers) round for round for 16:7, 16:7:0, 24:7, 4:3, 64:15, 16:1; parse
# refusals; wiring in multi._started and the engine. ALL PASS patched; FAILS on the synced tree.
# GB10: agentreplay.py (real agent turns) at PARALLEL 1, 2, 4, 6, 8, arms off / 16:7 / 16:7 + MISS_MAX=7, digests equal.
